# Line endings are LF in the repository and in every checkout, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. templates/run.sh is embedded in the binary and copied
# verbatim into every generated project, so a checkout that converted it to CRLF
# would produce projects whose task runner dies on its first line with
# "$'\r': command not found". The same goes for the commit-msg hook. Windows
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which is exactly where that would happen — and
# it would happen at build time, silently, with nothing in the diff to show it.
#
# It also keeps `gofmt -l` honest in CI on a Windows runner, which would otherwise
# report every Go file as unformatted.
* text=auto eol=lf
